.TH VELACUT 1 "October 2026" "velacut 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
velacut \- offline desktop video editor for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B velacut
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B velacut
is a desktop video editor for Linux, designed to be fast, simple, and completely local (no cloud, no account required).
.PP
Features include:
.IP \(bu 2
Timeline editing with magnetic tracks and automatic track creation
.IP \(bu 2
100+ transitions and 101 video effects
.IP \(bu 2
Text styles, animations, and keyframe support
.IP \(bu 2
Color correction with LUT, curves, and scopes
.IP \(bu 2
Audio mixing with LUFS normalization
.IP \(bu 2
Template projects with placeholders
.IP \(bu 2
Automatic saving (no "Save" button needed)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-safe\-mode
Start in software rendering mode (no GPU acceleration). Use if the app crashes on startup due to GPU driver issues.
.TP
.B \-\-component\-gallery
Show the Material 3 component gallery instead of the main application.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/velacut/
Application data directory containing drafts and user assets.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/velacut/packs/
User-installed asset packages (effects, transitions, templates).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/velacut/
Cache directory for GPU probes, thumbnails, and render jobs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/velacut/
Configuration files (graphics preferences, UI state).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B velacut
Start with the home screen showing existing drafts.
.TP
.B velacut video.mp4
Create a new project and import the video file.
.TP
.B velacut --safe-mode
Start in software rendering mode (fallback for GPU issues).
.TP
.B velacut project.vproj
Open an existing project file.
.SH PROJECT FORMAT
Projects are saved as
.I .vproj
files (JSON UTF-8). Saving is automatic every ~2 seconds. The format is human-readable and git-friendly.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Space
Play/Pause
.TP
.B S
Split clip at playhead
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Undo
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Z
Redo
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Universal search (effects, transitions, commands)
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Export video
.PP
See
.I /usr/share/doc/velacut/SHORTCUTS.md
for the complete list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QUICK_BACKEND=software
Force Qt Quick software rendering (same as --safe-mode).
.TP
.B LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1
Force Mesa software rendering.
